# Copy to deploy/agent.env and fill in, or let `pnpm tarfa setup` write it (`--help`).
# deploy/agent.env is gitignored.
# A strong random token, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. It authenticates Claude Code's hooks to the
# agent's loopback /hooks endpoint, and enrols a phone by token while token enrolment is on
# (`tarfa devices enrolment on`); a paired phone never holds it.
TARFA_TOKEN=replace-with-openssl-rand-hex-32
# Unique per machine (e.g. "mac" or "mini")
TARFA_MACHINE_ID=mac
# Colon-separated project roots offered for new workspaces
TARFA_PROJECT_ROOTS=/Users/you/workspace
# The loopback port Claude Code's hooks post to (install-hooks bakes it in). The agent listens on
# 127.0.0.1 only; phones never reach this port.
TARFA_PORT=8787
# The loopback port phones' WebSockets reach, once something publishes it (`tailscale serve`,
# Funnel, a reverse proxy). It serves upgrades only, on any path; never publish TARFA_PORT instead.
# Each agent on a machine needs its own (a second Linux user included).
TARFA_PHONE_PORT=8797
# Optional: where phones reach the phone port from outside, in the order a phone should try them
# (comma-separated wss:// URLs, at most 4). `tarfa pair` puts every one in its links, and
# `tarfa setup --tailscale serve|funnel` writes the Tailscale one. Logged at startup.
# TARFA_PHONE_ADDRESSES=wss://machine.tailnet.ts.net:10000/me
# Where phones open the PWA: the origin of the pairing links `tarfa pair` prints
# (default https://tarfa.app; set it for a PWA you serve yourself).
# TARFA_PWA_ORIGIN=https://pwa.example:8443
# Optional: the default path a pairing link gives a new phone entry, which relative New-workspace
# paths resolve against. Absolute (no ~), at most 128 characters; without it the link carries none.
# TARFA_DEFAULT_PATH=/Users/you/workspace
# Optional: the dictation vocabulary file (default ~/.tarfa/keyterms.txt).
# TARFA_KEYTERMS_PATH=/path/to/keyterms.txt
# Optional: `off` stops sending this machine's load (the RAM line on the phone's home screen),
# e.g. for a second Linux user on a machine whose load another agent already shows.
# TARFA_STATS=off
# Optional (Linux, Claude voice): the loopback subdevice this agent plays dictation into, when
# several users share the machine (docs/SETUP-MACHINE.md, step 11). Default plughw:Loopback,0.
# TARFA_VOICE_DEVICE=plughw:Loopback,0,1
